# Tailwind CSS Best Practices

This document outlines Tailwind CSS best practices for our project, focusing on maintainability, performance, and organization.

## Class Organization

- Follow a consistent order of utility classes (layout → typography → visual styles)
- Group related classes together for readability
- Use @apply in CSS files for recurring combinations of utility classes
- Extract component classes for complex, repeated UI elements
- Maintain consistent naming for custom components and utilities

## Custom Configuration

- Extend the theme in `tailwind.config.js` to maintain design system consistency
- Define custom colors, spacing, and typography settings in the config
- Use CSS variables for dynamic theming when appropriate
- Create custom variants for specific interactive states
- Implement design tokens through Tailwind's theme system

## Performance

- Enable JIT (Just-In-Time) mode for faster builds and smaller CSS output
- Use PurgeCSS properly by including all files with Tailwind classes in the purge configuration
- Optimize for production by removing unused styles
- Consider code splitting CSS for large applications
- Use responsive utilities judiciously to avoid CSS bloat

## Component Patterns

- Create reusable component classes with @apply for consistent styling
- Use Tailwind with CSS modules for component-specific styles when needed
- Implement responsive designs with Tailwind's responsive modifiers
- Leverage Tailwind's state variants for interactive elements

## Maintainability

- Document custom utilities and component classes
- Use consistent spacing and sizing scales
- Implement dark mode with Tailwind's dark variant
- Organize custom components in a logical structure
- Use plugins for specialized functionality

- Use utility classes directly in your JSX for rapid development.
- Create custom components with Tailwind classes for reusability.
- Utilize the `@apply` directive in CSS for complex, reusable styles.
- Implement responsive design using Tailwind's responsive utility classes. 
